-- Source text: Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), Act No. 23 of 2005, as enacted, from the unofficial plain-text rendering No.-23-of-2005.txt.
-- (c) Government of Ireland. Oireachtas Copyright Material is reproduced with the permission of the Houses of the Oireachtas.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS.
-- Four things about the text of an Act and how it is cited that ie-general.l4 does not hold:
-- s 7(1)(a), (b), (c): which text of an Act a court may look at, by kind of Act, for sections 5 and 6 (ie-general.l4 holds the coarse rule; this module
--   tells the three paragraphs apart and calls the coarse rule);
-- s 14(2): a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of the enactment as amended;
-- s 14(3): commas around a year in a citation that may be omitted;
-- s 15(2): the date of the passing that the Clerk of Dail Eireann endorses on the Act, and that is taken to be part of the Act.
--
-- WHAT THESE RULES MEAN FOR A PERSON. A person reading a citation can rely on it as a citation of the enactment as amended, whenever the amendment was made
-- (s 14(2)); can leave out the commas the section names (s 14(3)); can rely on the date endorsed on an Act as part of the Act (s 15(2)); and a person
-- who asks a court to read a provision of an Act under sections 5 or 6 knows which enrolled text the court may use (s 7(1)).
--
-- PRECONDITION, STATED ONCE (section 4(1)): as in the other modules, these functions assume that no contrary intention appears.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-general`

§ `Named refusals`

-- One definition per refusal; each name is its message.

-- src:154 | (2) Immediately after the Bill for an Act of the Oireachtas is signed by the President, the Clerk of Dáil Éireann shall endorse on the Act immediately after the long title the date of the passing of the Act, and that date shall be taken to be part of the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 15(2) (src:154)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 15(2) says immediately and gives no measure of time` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 15(2) says immediately and gives no measure of time"

-- src:153 | Date of passing of Acts of Oireachtas. 15.—(1) The date of the passing of an Act of the Oireachtas is the date of the day on which the Bill for the Act is signed by the President.
-- src:154 | (2) Immediately after the Bill for an Act of the Oireachtas is signed by the President, the Clerk of Dáil Éireann shall endorse on the Act immediately after the long title the date of the passing of the Act, and that date shall be taken to be part of the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 15(1) (src:153); s 15(2) (src:154)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 15(2) deems the date of the passing to be part of the Act and does not say what follows if a different date is endorsed` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 15(2) deems the date of the passing to be part of the Act and does not say what follows if a different date is endorsed"

§ `Section 7(1)(a), (b) and (c): the text a court may use for sections 5 and 6`

DECLARE `A kind of Act for section 7(1)` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)`
    `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)`
    `any other Act, paragraph (c)`

DECLARE `The text of an Act that section 7(1) names` IS ONE OF
    `the signed text as enrolled for record in the Office of the Registrar of the Supreme Court pursuant to Article 25.4.5 of the Constitution`
    `the signed text as enrolled for record in the office of the officer of the Supreme Court of Saorstat Eireann whom Dail Eireann determined pursuant to Article 42 of the Constitution of the Irish Free State`
    `such text of the Act as corresponds to the text enrolled in the manner referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)`

-- src:121 | (a) in the case of an Act of the Oireachtas, the signed text of such law as enrolled for record in the Office of the Registrar of the Supreme Court pursuant to Article 25.4.5° of the Constitution.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 7(1)(a) (src:121)
`the text that section 7(1)(a) names` MEANS
    `the signed text as enrolled for record in the Office of the Registrar of the Supreme Court pursuant to Article 25.4.5 of the Constitution`

-- src:122 | (b) in the case of an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstát Éireann, the signed text of such law as enrolled for record in the office of such officer of the Supreme Court of Saorstát Éireann as Dáil Éireann determined pursuant to Article 42 of the Constitution of the Irish Free State (Saorstát Éireann),
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 7(1)(b) (src:122)
`the text that section 7(1)(b) names` MEANS
    `the signed text as enrolled for record in the office of the officer of the Supreme Court of Saorstat Eireann whom Dail Eireann determined pursuant to Article 42 of the Constitution of the Irish Free State`

-- src:123 | (c) in the case of any other Act, such text of that Act as corresponds to the text of the Act enrolled in the manner referred to in paragraph (a) or (b).
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 7(1)(c) (src:123)
`the text that section 7(1)(c) names` MEANS
    `such text of the Act as corresponds to the text enrolled in the manner referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)`

-- src:120 | Supplemental provision to sections 5 and 6. 7.—(1) In construing a provision of an Act for the purposes of section 5 or 6 , a court may, notwithstanding section 18 (g), make use of all matters that accompany and are set out in—
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 7(1) (src:120)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of Act for section 7(1)`
GIVETH A `The text of an Act that section 7(1) names`
`the text of an Act that section 7(1) names for` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)`                   THEN `the text that section 7(1)(a) names`
    WHEN `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)` THEN `the text that section 7(1)(b) names`
    WHEN `any other Act, paragraph (c)`                              THEN `the text that section 7(1)(c) names`

-- F45: paragraphs (b) and (c) both concern an Act under limb (b) of the definition of "Act" in s 2(1) (a statute in force in Saorstat Eireann before the
-- Constitution and continued in force by Article 50); ie-general.l4 holds that class as `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force`.
-- src:120 | Supplemental provision to sections 5 and 6. 7.—(1) In construing a provision of an Act for the purposes of section 5 or 6 , a court may, notwithstanding section 18 (g), make use of all matters that accompany and are set out in—
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 7(1) (src:120)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of Act for section 7(1)`
GIVETH A `Kind of enactment`
`the kind of enactment, for section 7(1), of` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)`                   THEN `an Act of the Oireachtas`
    WHEN `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)` THEN `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force`
    WHEN `any other Act, paragraph (c)`                              THEN `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force`

-- src:120 | Supplemental provision to sections 5 and 6. 7.—(1) In construing a provision of an Act for the purposes of section 5 or 6 , a court may, notwithstanding section 18 (g), make use of all matters that accompany and are set out in—
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 7(1)(a), (b), (c) (src:120)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of Act for section 7(1)`
      `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter accompanies and is set out in the text that section 7(1) names for that kind of Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter, by the paragraph for the kind of Act` k `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` `the matter accompanies and is set out in the text that section 7(1) names for that kind of Act` MEANS
    `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` (`the kind of enactment, for section 7(1), of` k) `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` `the matter accompanies and is set out in the text that section 7(1) names for that kind of Act`

§ `Section 14(2): a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of the enactment as amended`

DECLARE `A way of changing an enactment` IS ONE OF
    amendment
    extension
    application
    adaptation
    `another modification`

DECLARE `When a change was made` IS ONE OF
    `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
    `on the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
    `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`

-- src:148 | (2) A citation of or a reference to an enactment shall be read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as amended (including as amended by way of extension, application, adaptation or other modification of the enactment), whether the amendment is made before, on or after the date on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 14(2) (src:148)
GIVEN `the day the change was made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `When a change was made`
`when the change was made, relative to the day the citing provision came into operation` `the day the change was made` `the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day the change was made` LESS THAN `the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
           THEN `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
           IF `the day the change was made` GREATER THAN `the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
           THEN `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`
           OTHERWISE `on the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`

-- src:148 | (2) A citation of or a reference to an enactment shall be read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as amended (including as amended by way of extension, application, adaptation or other modification of the enactment), whether the amendment is made before, on or after the date on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 14(2) (src:148)
GIVEN how IS A `A way of changing an enactment`
      w IS A `When a change was made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a citation of or reference to an enactment is read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as changed` how `, the change being made` w MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN amendment            THEN `the change counts whenever it was made` w
    WHEN extension            THEN `the change counts whenever it was made` w
    WHEN application          THEN `the change counts whenever it was made` w
    WHEN adaptation           THEN `the change counts whenever it was made` w
    WHEN `another modification` THEN `the change counts whenever it was made` w

-- "whether the amendment is made before, on or after the date on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation":
-- all three limbs give the same answer, so the one rule is stated once.
-- src:148 | (2) A citation of or a reference to an enactment shall be read as a citation of or reference to the enactment as amended (including as amended by way of extension, application, adaptation or other modification of the enactment), whether the amendment is made before, on or after the date on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 14(2) (src:148)
GIVEN w IS A `When a change was made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the change counts whenever it was made` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `before the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `on the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `after the day on which the provision containing the citation or reference came into operation`   THEN TRUE

§ `Section 14(3): commas around a year in a citation`

DECLARE `What is being cited` IS ONE OF
    `an Act, by its short title`
    `another enactment, by its citation`
    `something else, or in some other way`

DECLARE `Where a comma stands` IS ONE OF
    `immediately before a reference to a year`
    `immediately after a reference to a year`
    `elsewhere`

-- F39: "that is not required for the purpose of punctuation" is read as governing BOTH commas. See the fork register for the other reading.
-- src:149 | (3) In citing—
-- src:150 | (a) an Act by its short title, or
-- src:151 | (b) any other enactment by its citation (if any),
-- src:152 | a comma immediately before a reference to a year and a comma immediately after such a reference that is not required for the purpose of punctuation may be omitted.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 14(3) (src:149-152)
GIVEN what IS A `What is being cited`
      where IS A `Where a comma stands`
      `the comma is required for the purpose of punctuation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 14(3) lets the comma be omitted` what where `the comma is required for the purpose of punctuation` MEANS
    BRANCH IF what EQUALS `something else, or in some other way` THEN FALSE
           IF where EQUALS `elsewhere` THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOT `the comma is required for the purpose of punctuation`

§ `Section 15(2): the date of the passing is endorsed on the Act and is part of it`

-- F43: "Immediately after the Bill ... is signed" gives no measure of time, so the latest moment for the endorsement refuses; the date itself is answered.
-- F43 also: if a date other than the date of the passing is endorsed, the section deems the date of the passing to be part of the Act and says nothing of the other date; that refuses.

-- src:153 | Date of passing of Acts of Oireachtas. 15.—(1) The date of the passing of an Act of the Oireachtas is the date of the day on which the Bill for the Act is signed by the President.
-- src:154 | (2) Immediately after the Bill for an Act of the Oireachtas is signed by the President, the Clerk of Dáil Éireann shall endorse on the Act immediately after the long title the date of the passing of the Act, and that date shall be taken to be part of the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 15(2) (src:154) with s 15(1) (src:153)
GIVEN `the day the Bill was signed by the President` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the Clerk of Dail Eireann must endorse on the Act` `the day the Bill was signed by the President` MEANS
    `the date of the passing of an Act of the Oireachtas signed on` `the day the Bill was signed by the President`

-- src:153 | Date of passing of Acts of Oireachtas. 15.—(1) The date of the passing of an Act of the Oireachtas is the date of the day on which the Bill for the Act is signed by the President.
-- src:154 | (2) Immediately after the Bill for an Act of the Oireachtas is signed by the President, the Clerk of Dáil Éireann shall endorse on the Act immediately after the long title the date of the passing of the Act, and that date shall be taken to be part of the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 15(2) (src:154) with s 15(1) (src:153)
GIVEN `the day the Bill was signed by the President` IS A DATE
      `the date endorsed on the Act immediately after the long title` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the endorsed date is taken to be part of the Act` `the day the Bill was signed by the President` `the date endorsed on the Act immediately after the long title` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date endorsed on the Act immediately after the long title`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST e  THEN
        IF   e EQUALS `the date the Clerk of Dail Eireann must endorse on the Act` `the day the Bill was signed by the President`
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE `section 15(2) deems the date of the passing to be part of the Act and does not say what follows if a different date is endorsed`

-- src:154 | (2) Immediately after the Bill for an Act of the Oireachtas is signed by the President, the Clerk of Dáil Éireann shall endorse on the Act immediately after the long title the date of the passing of the Act, and that date shall be taken to be part of the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 15(2) (src:154)
GIVEN `the day the Bill was signed by the President` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATETIME
`the latest moment by which the Clerk of Dail Eireann must have endorsed the date` `the day the Bill was signed by the President` MEANS
    `section 15(2) says immediately and gives no measure of time`
